//! The Simplicity programs an order spends by, pruned, as sequentia-contracts
//! publishes them:
//!
//! - `templates/arca_order_3/fills.json`: `arca/order-3`, the fill of a
//!   resting order in the tree, which refuses an annex;
//! - `templates/seqdex_order_2/fills.json`: `seqdex/order` version 2, SeqDEX's
//!   order, which an `order-3` leaf lands as and which refuses an annex;
//! - `templates/arca_order/fills.json` and `templates/seqdex_order/fills.json`:
//!   `arca/order-2` and `seqdex/order` version 1, the same programs without
//!   that rule. An annex on one of their fills is bound by nothing, so whoever
//!   relays the fill can attach one; they are kept for the orders that rest
//!   under them until those are filled, landed or refunded.
//!
//! Each pruned program is one constant per path, whatever the order, so a
//! spend is built with no compiler. Copied byte for byte; the regtest tests
//! spend each one on the node.

